<article class="env-lemma" id="01EK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01EK">Lemma <span data-tag="01EK">20.10.2</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a ringed space. Let $\mathcal{U} : U = \bigcup _{i \in I} U_ i$ be an open covering. The functors $\mathcal{F} \mapsto \check{H}^ n(\mathcal{U}, \mathcal{F})$ form a $\delta $-functor from the abelian category of presheaves of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules to the category of $\mathcal{O}_ X(U)$-modules (see Homology, Definition <a href="/tag/010Q" data-tag="010Q">12.12.1</a>). </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/01EJ" data-tag="01EJ">20.10.1</a> a short exact sequence of presheaves of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules $0 \to \mathcal{F}_1 \to \mathcal{F}_2 \to \mathcal{F}_3 \to 0$ is turned into a short exact sequence of complexes of $\mathcal{O}_ X(U)$-modules. Hence we can use Homology, Lemma <a href="/tag/0117" data-tag="0117">12.13.12</a> to get the boundary maps $\delta _{\mathcal{F}_1 \to \mathcal{F}_2 \to \mathcal{F}_3} : \check{H}^ n(\mathcal{U}, \mathcal{F}_3) \to \check{H}^{n + 1}(\mathcal{U}, \mathcal{F}_1)$ and a corresponding long exact sequence. We omit the verification that these maps are compatible with maps between short exact sequences of presheaves. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>